00:02:19.335 --> 00:02:20.685
of people who have read the book.

00:02:21.225 --> 00:02:23.595
Uh, I sort of leafed through it.

00:02:24.375 --> 00:02:32.895
Um, my reaction is that he has sort of
this tremendous knowledge of psychology

00:02:32.895 --> 00:02:37.095
of, uh, mythology, of religion.

00:02:37.935 --> 00:02:46.350
And so he sort of describes, you
know, a world that our lives are in

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:50.519
his view, tragic or full of evil.

00:02:51.299 --> 00:02:55.480
I mean, eventually we die and there
are lots of bad things that happen.

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:57.750
Bad things have always happened.

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:04.380
And so in this world of chaos,
then how should we lead our lives?

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:10.400
Uh, in his first chapter, which
he calls uh, you know, stand up

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:11.760
straight with your shoulders back.

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:16.110
In other words, you should have a very
erect posture and it ties that in some

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:23.100
